  "metadata": {
    "title": "Positive tangent-bundle Seshadri constants characterize projective space",
    "upload_type": "publication",
    "publication_type": "preprint",
    "publication_date": "2026-10-12",
    "creators": [
      {
        "name": "Kriebel, Alec",
        "affiliation": "Independent researcher",
        "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"
      }
    ],
    "description": "<p>Let X be a smooth integral projective variety of dimension n at least one over an algebraically closed field of arbitrary characteristic. Positivity of the relative Fulger-Murayama Seshadri constant of the tangent bundle at one arbitrary closed point implies that X is projective n-space. The five-page research note proves Fulger-Murayama Conjecture 4.9 without assuming Fano, global tangent nefness, characteristic zero, or a general point.</p><p>An absolute minimum of ample degree through the specified point eliminates the boundary of the one-marked stable-map family. Very-free evaluation and the actual contracted marking section give numerical Picard rank one and ampleness of the anticanonical divisor; the established Fano clause completes the proof. Standard numerical-generation methods, Mori/Kollar, Fulger-Murayama, and Chang's toric case are credited. The source and verification archive preserves the frozen original candidate, independent mathematical reviews, a documented 64-query priority audit, and portable integrity and finite controls. Those computations do not formally verify the geometric theorem.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in developing, checking, reviewing, and preparing the result. This is an unrefereed preprint; internal AI-assisted review is not external human peer review. A bounded primary-source audit found no earlier full resolution, but first historical priority is not certified. The full Kollar monograph and CMSB text were not independently obtained; the exact imported published Fulger-Murayama propositions were inspected. The deposit is licensed CC BY 4.0.</p>",
    "access_right": "open",
    "license": "cc-by-4.0",
    "version": "1.0",
    "language": "eng",
    "keywords": [
      "Seshadri constants",
      "tangent bundle",
      "projective space",
